cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Multimodal Framework for Electricity Price Forecasting Using
  Sentiment-Augmented Time-Series Signals
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rohan
    family-names: Fozdar
    affiliation: Knox College
abstract: >-
  A forecasting framework for next-hour ERCOT real-time hub-average electricity
  prices and for flagging price spikes above $200/MWh. Eight data sources,
  spanning prices, system load, weather, natural gas, nuclear outages and GDELT
  news sentiment, are combined into an hourly matrix of 77,956 observations and
  87 engineered features covering 2016 to 2024. Thirteen model configurations
  are benchmarked under one chronological split; a hybrid that feeds a frozen
  Chronos forecast into XGBoost performs best, at $12.13/MWh mean absolute
  error with 61.4% spike recall on the held-out 2024 test year.
keywords:
  - electricity price forecasting
  - ERCOT
  - price spikes
  - time series foundation models
  - news sentiment
  - gradient boosting
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/rohanfozdar/Electricity-Spot-Price-Forecaster
url: https://rohanfozdar.github.io/Electricity-Spot-Price-Forecaster/
year: 2026
